       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Per dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single oral dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Per day:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for inpatients is 3,200 mg/day, so this is double that. It raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours:** a typical dose for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg total per day, divided:** for example, 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical reason. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
